      "486b0a7c",
      "Homepage Builder",
      false,
      "high",
      "This may seem like overkill but I would like you to section off the directory structure of this app based on its features such as task, notes, page building and links.\n\nI want you to give each section their own MFDB and the baseline fields for all of them should be the same such as things like category type key path whatever the f*** it is If they can be cross used then use the same fields for all of them to try to keep the database as similar as possible also keep everything human readable all variables all names all pass everything as we can read all \n\nThe task management will be powered by its own MFTB he essentially gave each category it's own entity. \n\nMake sure whenever possible if you can use the same field for different things like the links you might use category for both links and tasks make sure you put those categories like first those fields first in the schemas and try to meet the schemas as a line as possible at first and then differ. Even the app gets its own MFDB and it's actually the master MFDB the rest for slaves\n\n\n/data/mfdb\n\n\n/content/tasks/data/mfdb\ncontent/tasks/categories\n\n/content/links/data/mfdb\ncontent/links/categories\n\ncontent/build/data/mfdb\ncontent/build/categories\n\ncontent/notes/data/mfdb\ncontent/notes/categories\n\nNOT JUST THIS APP BUT THIS WILL BE THE WAY THAT THE NEW WEB FRAMEWORK IS BUILT EVERY COMPONENT YOU DROP FOR A SECTION OR EVERY NEW SECTION YOU'LL HAVE A PAGE FOR IT YOU'LL HAVE A CATEGORY YOU'LL HAVE A DATABASE AND IT'LL ALL JUST BE SCAFFOLDED OUT READY TO GO PLEASE SECTION\n\nFeel free to create new very families just don't alter my current libraries you can import them and create new families like for the for this specific app if you want I would and that way you can separate concerns and you can start building the web framework library actually that would be best.\n\nI saw the homepage will be getting its own database I'll tell you why later on our new landing page but it will be the master. \n\nThere will also be one final other database and it's going to be for our web framework but I'll also explain later but to give you a hit it will basically be for storeing the architecture of sailing you lay down a section right You lay down and note sectionable It drops here HTML component and drops you CSS component and it drops a scaffolded MFTV database That's the goal of the future framework later so we're going to need an MFDB to actually hold the components in CSS the logic to build the databases with them. We will get there Don't think too much about it we're not there yet.",
